  "section": "Movie Facts # 8 of 10",
  "description": "George Lucas admitted in the documentary Empire of Dreams that he was on the set of Return of the Jedi more often than he originally expected due to director Richard Marquand's relative inexperience with special effects. Even so, The Empire Strikes Back helmer Irvin Kershner has stated in DVD commentaries that Lucas, who acted more as a hands-on advisor on Empire, most likely functioned in similar fashion on Jedi. Kershner also mentioned that the Star Wars creator considers The Empire Strikes Back Kershner's movie, not his."
